# Runsten configuration for compose.yaml. Copy it, fill it in, keep it private:
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# .env is ignored by git. The binaries validate this configuration when they start:
# a mistake stops them with a message (docker compose logs api collector).
# The users of runsten-api are not configured here: once the stack runs, create the
# first one with "docker compose run --rm api user create <name>" (README).
# A value containing "$" must be written between single quotes ('…'), otherwise
# Compose interpolates it.

# --- Release ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# The release of the images (ghcr.io/runsten-app/runsten-*), as on the releases page:
# 0.4.1 stays on it, 0.4 follows its fixes; empty, latest. Back up before changing it
# (README, Updating), then: docker compose pull && docker compose up -d
RUNSTEN_VERSION=

# --- Database ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both are only read when the PostgreSQL volume is created: changing them later does
# not change the passwords (ALTER ROLE in psql does). Hexadecimal keeps them URL-safe:
#   openssl rand -hex 24
# The superuser, never used by Runsten:
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# runsten, the application user (not a superuser):
RUNSTEN_DB_PASSWORD=

# --- Token encryption key ---------------------------------------------------------
# 32 random bytes in base64, used to encrypt the Volvo tokens stored in the database:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# It is never stored. Keep a copy apart from the backups: without it, the stored
# tokens cannot be decrypted, and the Volvo ID has to be connected again. The data
# (snapshots, trips, charges) is not encrypted with it and is not lost.
RUNSTEN_TOKEN_KEY=

# --- Volvo application ------------------------------------------------------------
# Your own application, from https://developer.volvocars.com/ (README, "Connecting a
# Volvo"). The client secret never leaves the backend.
# The application key (vcc-api-key) reads every vehicle of the instance. Left empty,
# the instance has none (as the hosted offer): each account gives the key of an
# application of its own on the Connection page.
RUNSTEN_VOLVO_API_KEY=
RUNSTEN_VOLVO_CLIENT_ID=
RUNSTEN_VOLVO_CLIENT_SECRET=
# The redirect URI registered with the application, which cannot be changed once it
# is published. It must lead to /auth/volvo/callback on the host where you sign in:
# runsten-web, which relays it to runsten-api (https there also makes the session
# cookie Secure):
# - behind a reverse proxy: https://runsten.example.org/auth/volvo/callback;
# - on the host itself (or through an SSH tunnel), if Volvo accepts it (not verified):
#   http://127.0.0.1:8082/auth/volvo/callback.
RUNSTEN_VOLVO_REDIRECT_URI=
# Scopes granted to the application, space separated, if it does not have all the
# default read scopes (the README lists them; location:read reportedly requires a
# review by Volvo).
# RUNSTEN_VOLVO_SCOPES=openid conve:vehicle_relation conve:odometer_status …

# --- Ports on the host (always bound to 127.0.0.1) ---------------------------------
# RUNSTEN_WEB_PORT=8082   the web interface: the one to put behind the reverse proxy
# RUNSTEN_API_PORT=8081   runsten-api alone: its minimal pages, scripts
# RUNSTEN_DEBUG_PORT=8090

# --- Web interface ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Public prefix, when the reverse proxy serves Runsten under a path and strips it
# (https://example.org/runsten/ → RUNSTEN_WEB_BASE_PATH=/runsten/). Default: /.
# RUNSTEN_WEB_BASE_PATH=
# Maps (trips, the vehicle's position, places): the raster tiles, a URL with {z}, {x}
# and {y}. Off by default: the browser fetches the tiles itself, so their provider sees
# its address and the areas shown. OpenStreetMap's own tiles suit a personal instance
# (https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/); beyond, take a provider.
# RUNSTEN_WEB_MAP_TILES=https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
# The attribution the provider requires, as plain text. Default: © OpenStreetMap contributors.
# RUNSTEN_WEB_MAP_ATTRIBUTION=
# true: every response asks search engines not to index it (X-Robots-Tag), for an
# instance on the internet that should not be found. Default: false.
# RUNSTEN_WEB_NOINDEX=

# --- Addresses --------------------------------------------------------------------
# A reverse geocoder speaking Nominatim's API names the positions outside your places
# (a street and a town). Off by default: runsten-api then sends it those positions, one
# per interval. OpenStreetMap's own suits a personal instance, at one request per second
# (https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/nominatim/); beyond, take a provider
# or run a Nominatim of your own.
# RUNSTEN_GEOCODER_URL=https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org
# RUNSTEN_GEOCODER_INTERVAL=1s

# --- MQTT -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Each account sets its broker in the settings (Settings → MQTT), never here. By
# default Runsten publishes to a broker on your own network, in plain mqtt:// or over
# TLS. false: brokers on the Internet only, over TLS (mqtts://), never a loopback,
# private or link-local address, checked again at each connection; for an instance
# whose users are not all trusted, so that a broker URL cannot reach the server's
# network. Read by api (the settings) and collector (the connections).
# RUNSTEN_MQTT_PRIVATE_BROKERS=true
# With the mqtt profile (docker compose --profile mqtt up -d), a Mosquitto broker for
# trying it out, on 127.0.0.1 of the host: mqtt://mosquitto:1883 in the settings.
# RUNSTEN_MQTT_PORT=1883

# --- Health report ----------------------------------------------------------------
# GET /healthz/full on runsten-api, for an uptime monitor: whether the database has
# connections left and the collector passes over the vehicles, 503 when not. Off by
# default; on, it asks for this token (Authorization: Bearer …), 32 characters at least:
# openssl rand -base64 32. Reach it through your reverse proxy.
# RUNSTEN_HEALTH_TOKEN=

# --- Collector --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Debug page: vehicle states and the last API calls, with VINs and locations. Off by
# default. 0.0.0.0 is the container's side; on the host, it stays on 127.0.0.1.
# RUNSTEN_DEBUG_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8090
# Polling and token lifecycle (defaults: 10s, 10m, 1m, 1h, 24h, 2m, 24h).
# RUNSTEN_POLL_TICK=10s
# RUNSTEN_POLL_PARKED=10m
# RUNSTEN_POLL_ACTIVE=1m
# RUNSTEN_POLL_RARE=1h
# RUNSTEN_POLL_DETAILS=24h
# RUNSTEN_TOKEN_MARGIN=2m
# RUNSTEN_TOKEN_KEEPALIVE=24h
# Calls a day per API granted to your Volvo application (default 10000): the collector
# spreads 90 % of it over the day.
# RUNSTEN_VOLVO_DAILY_QUOTA=10000
# true if Volvo counts that quota per user (Volvo ID) rather than per application.
# RUNSTEN_VOLVO_QUOTA_PER_USER=false

# debug, info, warn or error (default info).
# RUNSTEN_LOG_LEVEL=info
